.TH USB-UNLOCK-ON 1 "July 2026" "gway-001" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usb-unlock-on \- mount the verified bastion unlock USB read-only
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-unlock-on
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usb-unlock-on
searches USB block partitions for a bastion unlock layout containing
.I bastion/unlock.pass
or
.IR bastion-ssh/unlock.pass .
When found, it mounts that partition read-only at
.I /mnt/bastion-unlock
and prints the directory containing
.IR unlock.pass .
.P
Already-mounted non-target USB partitions are skipped during probing so
unrelated removable media is not unmounted. If a desktop automounter already
mounted a bastion directory under
.I /media
or
.IR /run/media ,
the existing mount can be used.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /mnt/bastion-unlock
Read-only bastion unlock mount point.
.TP
.I /mnt/bastion-unlock.probe
Temporary probe mount point.
.TP
.I /run/bastion-ssh/refresh.disabled
Hold file that disables refresh while sensitive USB operations are in progress.
.SH SAFETY
The mounted bastion key is read-only, nosuid, nodev, and noexec. The command
does not print the unlock password.
